!! warning[plan/cross-client-agent]: `security-reviewer`: Cursor also loads it from .claude/agents/, has no per-tool allow-list, and how it treats a Claude Code agent's `tools` is undocumented, so it may get all of the parent agent's tools; GitHub Copilot (CLI and VS Code) also loads it from .claude/agents/, and how it maps Claude Code tool names and `disallowedTools` is undocumented
!! warning[plan/cross-client-agent]: `silent-reviewer`: Cursor also loads it from .claude/agents/, has no per-tool allow-list, and how it treats a Claude Code agent's `tools` is undocumented, so it may get all of the parent agent's tools; GitHub Copilot (CLI and VS Code) also loads it from .claude/agents/, and how it maps Claude Code tool names and `disallowedTools` is undocumented
!! warning[plan/cross-client-hooks]: Cursor and GitHub Copilot also run hooks from .claude/settings.json, so `secret-guard`'s hooks run there too; whether they pass `args` and honor `onFailure` is undocumented, so there a hook may let actions through when it fails, or block every tool call if its arguments are dropped (turn off Claude Code hooks in that client to recover)
!! warning[plan/cross-client-mcp]: GitHub Copilot (VS Code and CLI) also starts servers listed in .mcp.json, so `docs-index` is available there too
